# 04-BRD / brand

**Goes here.** What the brand stands for, and how it looks and speaks. Positioning,
naming, distinctiveness, category entry points, verbal identity, visual identity,
brand book structure, and the consumer psychology of why people choose a brand.

## Not here

- Page copy principles and section structure -> 07-LPG
- Copywriting craft -> 11-ADC
- What the customer says in their own words -> 02-AVT
- Creative patterns and hooks -> 10-MCR
- Growing an audience and posting cadence -> 13-ORG
- A founder's full story across offer, creative and brand -> 99-multi

**The BRD and ORG line.** What the brand stands for is BRD. How you distribute it is
ORG. Seth Godin on permission and audience is positioning philosophy, so it is BRD.

**Lesson from misfiles.** Positioning and naming sources were filed in 21-OPS, and
brand psychology sources in 13-ORG. Anything about what the brand means or is called
belongs here.

